### 7.3 Inertial Sensing
{% if sensing.inertial_sensing.imu.present -%}
- **{{ sensing.inertial_sensing.imu.axes }}-axis IMU** — gyroscope + accelerometer
- Mounting: {{ sensing.inertial_sensing.imu.mounting_location }}
- {{ "Magnetometer included" if sensing.inertial_sensing.imu.magnetometer else "**No magnetometer**" }} — brushed DC motors make indoor magnetic heading unreliable; relative yaw is recovered from leg odometry against the planted foot, with slow absolute-yaw drift accepted
- IMU is **included in MVS cost accounting**
- Rationale: pelvis orientation and centre-of-mass velocity are required feedback states for every model-based balance method this design targets, and are not observable from joint encoders and foot force/torque alone
{%- else -%}
- No inertial sensing in the MVS
{%- endif %}

### 7.4 End-of-Limb Force/Torque Sensing
- Each foot includes a **6-DOF force/torque sensor**
